Guard GermplasmAttributeUpdateRightsMigration against an empty bulkWrite.

The 1.5.1 migration builds a list of Mongo UpdateOneModel ops from the
germplasm attribute collection and calls attributeCollection.bulkWrite(ops)
unconditionally. When the collection is empty (no germplasm has custom
attributes) the ops list is empty and the Mongo driver throws
"IllegalArgumentException: state should be: writes is not an empty list",
aborting the migration instead of completing as a no-op.

Present in 1.5.4 and still unfixed on upstream develop as of 2026-09-01.
Reported upstream: TODO(link).

--- a/opensilex-migration/src/main/java/org/opensilex/migration/one_point_five_ALL/GermplasmAttributeUpdateRightsMigration.java
+++ b/opensilex-migration/src/main/java/org/opensilex/migration/one_point_five_ALL/GermplasmAttributeUpdateRightsMigration.java
@@ -101,6 +101,10 @@
             ));
         }

+        if (ops.isEmpty()) {
+            logger.info("No germplasm attribute documents to update, skipping bulk write");
+            return;
+        }
         attributeCollection.bulkWrite(session, ops);
     }

